# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 1.4575e+03 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 1.2780 85.271 2.0459e+04 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~85 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 Y first_yield 2.7630 68.183 7.5105e+05 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 0.04 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 F flare 2.7837 67.945 1.5370e+06 stylized  Light rises x4.2 in 0.12 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 68.1 km (100% of m0); split gen 0 at 67.6 km (99% of m0). Dust groups supply 25% of the rise and 19% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
5 B first_breakup 2.8081 67.666 3.1697e+06 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x4.2 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
6 P peak 4.7311 46.480 1.4996e+07 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+3.2 km from the peak of energy deposition (43.2 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 17.1 km/s).
7 - drag_overtakes_ablation 5.4001 40.257 9.1330e+06 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
8 D rolloff 5.6581 38.214 5.5147e+06 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.93 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 65% of v0, 34% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
9 T tail 7.3291 30.383 1.4811e+04 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
10 R retirement_step 7.7461 29.437 2.4859e+03 artifact  A group is removed because it slowed below v_dark = 3.0 km/s; the light drops 29% within 0.03 s. A bookkeeping step, not a physical dimming.
